  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3413 (head b38f0c12f). These items are owed tests and one small path fault. They are not defects of the protection.\n\n1. No test measures the swept cutter disc against the protected item. The app pin (`crates/app/tests/do_not_touch_face.rs:178-187`) checks centre points at flute radius plus clearance, and it samples an arc only on the straight line between its ends. Add a pin with the shape-mask helper (`crates/motion/tests/common/shape_mask.rs`).\n2. No pin covers a Face with protected items in a rotated setup, or under a 3+2 frame.\n3. No pin covers a lower level that is clipped more than the level above it.\n4. When row 0 of a level is fully blocked, the level plunges at the start point, lifts, and plunges again at the same point (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/face.rs:258` and `:277-284`). The move is safe and not necessary. Remove it and pin the move count.\n5. The hole note can fire when only the keep-out caused the lift.\n",
